# xArtify Art Platform - AI Agent Rules

## Project Overview
xArtify is a Bulgarian art platform built with Next.js 15, featuring:
- Art gallery with paintings from artists
- Online courses and materials
- Artist profiles and artwork management
- E-commerce with Stripe payments
- Admin dashboard for platform management
- Mobile-first responsive design with grayscale + neon theme

## Core Technologies & Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 15.5.2 with App Router
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM
- **Authentication**: NextAuth.js v4 with multiple providers
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4 with custom CSS modules
- **Payments**: Stripe integration
- **Image Storage**: Cloudinary
- **Rate Limiting**: Upstash Redis
- **Email**: Resend
- **Deployment**: Vercel

## TypeScript & Code Quality Rules

### Strict Typing Requirements
- **🚨 CRITICAL: NEVER use `any` type** - always provide explicit types
- **🚨 MANDATORY: NO `any` under any circumstances** - this wastes tokens and creates errors
- Use `interface` for object shapes, `type` for unions/primitives
- Always type function parameters and return values
- Use generic types for reusable components
- Prefer `const assertions` for immutable data
- Use `satisfies` operator for type checking without widening

### Component Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Correct component typing
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  isVisible: boolean;
  onAction: (id: string) => void;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export default function Component({ title, isVisible, onAction, children }: ComponentProps): JSX.Element {
  // Implementation
}

// ❌ Never do this
function Component(props: any) {
  // Implementation
}
```

### API Route Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Correct API route typing
export async function GET(): Promise<NextResponse> {
  try {
    const data = await prisma.model.findMany();
    return NextResponse.json(data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
    return NextResponse.json({ message: 'Error occurred' }, { status: 500 });
  }
}
```

## Security Best Practices

### Authentication & Authorization
- Always check session in protected routes: `const session = await getServerSession(authOptions)`
- Use role-based access control: `session?.user?.role === "ADMIN"`
- Implement rate limiting on all API endpoints
- Validate all inputs with Zod schemas
- Use CSRF protection and secure headers

### **CRITICAL: RLS Policy Requirement**
- **MANDATORY**: When creating or refactoring CRUD functionality requiring authorization, ALWAYS provide corresponding SQL RLS policies
- This ensures double-layer security: application-level auth + database-level RLS
- **RLS Policy Location**: ALL RLS policies MUST be stored in `@supabasePolicies/` directory
- **Policy Discovery**: When checking existing RLS policies, ALWAYS look in `@supabasePolicies/` folder first
- **New Policy Creation**: When creating new RLS policies, save them in `@supabasePolicies/` directory with descriptive filename
- **CRITICAL: Schema Validation**: ALWAYS check `prisma/schema.prisma` before creating SQL policies to ensure:
  - Correct table names (check `@@map` directives)
  - Correct column names (camelCase vs snake_case)
  - Proper relationships and foreign keys
  - Model field types and constraints
- Include the SQL policies as `.sql` files or code blocks for direct database injection
- Example pattern for every protected resource:

```sql
-- Enable RLS on table
ALTER TABLE table_name ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Create policies for each operation
CREATE POLICY "policy_name_select" ON table_name
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid()::text = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "policy_name_insert" ON table_name
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid()::text = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "policy_name_update" ON table_name
  FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid()::text = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "policy_name_delete" ON table_name
  FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid()::text = user_id);
```

### **MANDATORY: Documentation Requirement**
- **ALWAYS create `.md` documentation files** when creating or refactoring new functionality
- Document the complete functionality including:
  - Purpose and overview
  - API endpoints and their parameters
  - Database schema changes
  - Security considerations and RLS policies
  - Usage examples and integration patterns
  - Error handling and edge cases
- Place documentation in appropriate directories (e.g., `docs/`, component-specific folders)
- Keep documentation up-to-date with code changes

### Data Validation
```typescript
// ✅ Always validate with Zod
import { z } from "zod";

const CreatePaintingSchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1).max(140),
  price: z.number().positive(),
  images: z.array(z.string().url()).min(1).max(10),
});

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const body = await req.json();
  const validatedData = CreatePaintingSchema.parse(body);
  // Process validated data
}
```

### Security Headers
- CSP with nonce-based script execution
- HSTS in production
- X-Frame-Options: DENY
- Content-Type-Options: nosniff
- Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

## Mobile-First UX Guidelines

### Responsive Design
- **Mobile-first approach**: Design for mobile, enhance for desktop
- Use Tailwind's mobile-first breakpoints: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`
- Touch-friendly button sizes (minimum 44px)
- Optimize for thumb navigation
- Implement proper viewport meta tag

### Performance Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component with optimization
- Implement lazy loading for images
- Use SWR for data fetching with caching
- Minimize bundle size with dynamic imports
- Implement proper loading states and skeletons

### Mobile UX Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ Mobile-optimized component
export default function MobileOptimizedComponent(): JSX.Element {
  const [isMobile, setIsMobile] = useState(false);
  
  useEffect(() => {
    const mq = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 767px)");
    setIsMobile(mq.matches);
    mq.addEventListener("change", (e) => setIsMobile(e.matches));
  }, []);

  return (
    <div className="p-4 md:p-8">
      <button className="w-full md:w-auto min-h-[44px] touch-manipulation">
        Mobile-friendly button
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

